item.description:
WNC Sierra Club
Join us Oct. 7 as Ken Brame, who serves as the WNC Sierra Club Political Co-Chair, talks about what's at stake in the 2026 midterm elections. His presentation will cover what's happening nationally, in North Carolina, and locally. Learn more about:

* Which races will be most competitive;
* What the political climate looks like;
* What the potential outcomes are;
* The implications for the environment;
* How you can get involved and make a difference.

Ken Brame is the former chair of both the national Sierra Club Political Committee and the NC Sierra Club Political Committee.

The WNC Sierra Club meets monthly in Room 102 at UNCA’s Reuter Center on Campus Drive and simultaneously on [Zoom](https://unca-edu.zoom.us/j/85189349413?pwd=QmorsXPwjbS0BgiLR7xLItF3M1atab.1).

**Parking at UNC Asheville:** If you do not have a parking sticker from OLLI, you'll need to register for parking either ahead of time at [unca.aimsparking.com](https://unca.aimsparking.com/) or at the Reu
